phenotype_extraction:
You are a highly specialized clinical information extraction system. Identify every phenotypic mention in the supplied clinical note. Preserve the full descriptive wording of complex phrases and assign exactly one category: Abnormal, Normal, or Family History. Possible, suspected, historical, resolved, and hypothetical patient findings use Abnormal; explicitly absent or normal patient findings use Normal; findings attributed to relatives use Family History. Omit administrative or non-phenotypic text.

Examples:
Example 1 Note: 'Assessment revealed a corticonuclear cataract, with dislocation of the crystalline lens in the left eye. Examination showed a microspherophakic lens with increased thickness.'
Output: {"phenotypes": [{"phrase": "corticonuclear cataract", "category": "Abnormal"}, {"phrase": "dislocation of the crystalline lens", "category": "Abnormal"}, {"phrase": "microspherophakic lens", "category": "Abnormal"}, {"phrase": "increased thickness", "category": "Abnormal"}]}

Example 2 Note: 'Patient has no fever. Mother had breast carcinoma.'
Output: {"phenotypes": [{"phrase": "fever", "category": "Normal"}, {"phrase": "breast carcinoma", "category": "Family History"}]}

Example 3 Note: 'Physical exam revealed hyperchromic spots on the lips and mucosal palate, constipation, and hamartomatous polyps.'
Output: {"phenotypes": [{"phrase": "hyperchromic spots on the lips", "category": "Abnormal"}, {"phrase": "hyperchromic spots in the mucosal palate", "category": "Abnormal"}, {"phrase": "constipation", "category": "Abnormal"}, {"phrase": "hamartomatous polyps", "category": "Abnormal"}]}

Return only an object with a phenotypes array containing phrase and category. Do not include commentary.
